WEBVTT

00:00:02.890 --> 00:00:05.630
Not a day goes by in Paris without someone

00:00:05.630 --> 00:00:09.380
mentioning the name of Mr. Shinomiya Kojirou, the chef of SHINO'S.

00:00:09.380 --> 00:00:11.440
Now he's opening his first
 restaurant in Japan, in Tokyo.

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:15.240
Gourmands have mounting expectations for Mr. Shinomiya's dishes,

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:18.030
as he is called the Magician of Legumes.

00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:19.410
Huh?

00:00:19.990 --> 00:00:22.620
I barely get any sleep getting ready for the opening.

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:26.660
That's exactly why Chef Doujima suggested sending over a student

00:00:26.660 --> 00:00:29.590
to serve as your opening staff. 
It'd be mutually beneficial.

00:00:31.110 --> 00:00:35.020
I'm sure you would be happy to cooperate,

00:00:35.020 --> 00:00:39.010
given that the request is coming from me,
 a sad hired chef at Tohtsuki.

00:00:39.010 --> 00:00:40.690
So he said.

00:00:40.690 --> 00:00:42.980
<i>How long are you going to be ticked about that?!</i>

00:00:43.380 --> 00:00:45.240
What would you know about any of this?!

00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:48.480
You're a hired chef for the Tohtsuki Group!

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:54.610
I won't accept anyone less than one of the Autumn Selection finalists.

00:00:54.610 --> 00:00:55.850
'Sup!

00:00:59.950 --> 00:01:03.130
Thanks for having me, 
Shinomiya-senpai.

00:01:03.960 --> 00:02:34.000
{OP}

00:01:18.690 --> 00:01:28.610
Far beyond the image I have in my mind

00:01:28.610 --> 00:01:35.080
The reality I'm building up is still far away

00:01:35.740 --> 00:01:38.830
An endless journey

00:01:38.830 --> 00:01:43.840
Let's hone each other's pride

00:01:43.840 --> 00:01:46.340
Words aren't really important

00:01:46.340 --> 00:01:48.840
So let's just say "yes" and leave it at that

00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:55.810
We fight each other and hone our skills

00:01:58.180 --> 00:02:00.690
Our encounters cause shockwaves

00:02:00.690 --> 00:02:03.440
We're reckless challengers

00:02:03.440 --> 00:02:08.440
Heading toward a world as yet unexplored

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:10.990
A swordsman should use his blade

00:02:10.990 --> 00:02:13.820
To open the way to the future

00:02:13.820 --> 00:02:19.540
This is my story and no one else's

00:02:35.650 --> 00:02:39.990
I wasn't expecting you, of all people, Yukihira.

00:02:39.990 --> 00:02:42.620
Yeah, I was surprised too!

00:02:42.620 --> 00:02:44.390
I didn't think I'd end up in your restaurant.

00:02:45.060 --> 00:02:47.660
<i>I'll be in Shinomiya Kojirou's kitchen.</i>

00:02:47.660 --> 00:02:52.640
<i>Not to mention, I need to make a visible mark
 if I'm gonna pass the Stagiaire.</i>

00:02:52.640 --> 00:02:56.030
<i>It won't be easy, but I'll do it.</i>

00:02:56.900 --> 00:02:59.780
First, you'll be wrapping up
 construction and interior work.

00:02:59.780 --> 00:03:02.070
<i>Huh? They're still at </i>that<i> stage?</i>

00:03:02.070 --> 00:03:04.030
Hurry up and work!

00:03:04.030 --> 00:03:05.120
Do you want to get fired?!

00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:05.700
Got it!

00:03:06.180 --> 00:03:07.450
Chef Shinomiya!

00:03:07.830 --> 00:03:10.830
We have to create the menu at the same time too.

00:03:10.830 --> 00:03:12.280
That's right!

00:03:12.280 --> 00:03:14.460
We should ask contractors!

00:03:14.870 --> 00:03:19.010
Considering our remaining budget, we'll do what we can on our own.

00:03:19.010 --> 00:03:22.600
I was very choosy about things
 like the interior and the dishware.

00:03:22.600 --> 00:03:25.530
But Chef Shinomiya, you could 
get any budget you want.

00:03:25.530 --> 00:03:27.100
You have the Pluspol Award.

00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:31.410
All the sponsors who backed my flagship restaurant
 have opposed opening this restaurant.

00:03:31.410 --> 00:03:33.230
I can't ask them for money.

00:03:33.230 --> 00:03:35.500
Jeez! You're too proud!

00:03:35.500 --> 00:03:37.650
The pre-open is tomorrow.

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:39.720
Oh, sorry.

00:03:39.720 --> 00:03:42.320
We're staff from SHINO'S, 
the flagship restaurant.

00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:46.920
We're here to support the Tokyo restaurant until things settle down after it opens!

00:03:46.920 --> 00:03:47.490
Right!

00:03:47.490 --> 00:03:48.910
Nice to meet you!

00:03:48.910 --> 00:03:53.800
He's the head chef 
of SHINO'S Tokyo, Abel Blondin.

00:03:53.800 --> 00:03:56.200
He was the sous chef in the main restaurant,

00:03:56.200 --> 00:03:58.460
so he's Chef Shinomiya's right-hand man.

00:03:58.460 --> 00:03:59.670
Nice to meet you.

00:03:59.670 --> 00:04:01.540
Sure, hi.

00:04:01.540 --> 00:04:02.680
Well, good luck.

00:04:02.680 --> 00:04:05.570
Hey, cut the chatter!

00:04:05.570 --> 00:04:07.120
Yukihira, come over here.

00:04:07.120 --> 00:04:07.850
Got it!

00:04:08.340 --> 00:04:11.120
Opening a restaurant's tough, huh?

00:04:11.120 --> 00:04:14.840
Well, I'm lucky I get to train at your restaurant, Senpai.

00:04:14.840 --> 00:04:16.520
Shut up and just carry the cabinet!

00:04:16.900 --> 00:04:18.460
<i>What's with him?</i>

00:04:18.460 --> 00:04:21.110
<i>He's acting so familiar with Chef Shinomiya!</i>

00:04:21.630 --> 00:04:25.450
<i>He has no idea how long it took me
 to get friendly with Chef Shinomiya!</i>

00:04:25.890 --> 00:04:29.450
And when he finally picked me to be the head chef of the Tokyo restaurant,

00:04:29.830 --> 00:04:33.120
I've never been more 
profoundly moved in my life!

00:04:33.120 --> 00:04:34.000
Yeah, yeah.

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:36.170
It's only the millionth 
time you've told us that.

00:04:36.170 --> 00:04:39.740
But Chef Shinomiya's gotten 
pretty mellow, hasn't he?

00:04:39.740 --> 00:04:41.720
Did the change happen after 
he went to Japan in spring?

00:04:41.720 --> 00:04:42.720
Could be.

00:04:42.720 --> 00:04:44.760
He was some kind of judge, right?

00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:47.220
I think he became a bit nicer when he got back.

00:04:47.590 --> 00:04:50.530
He'll teach you with patience if you ask him about cooking too.

00:04:50.530 --> 00:04:51.560
Yeah, right?

00:04:51.560 --> 00:04:53.940
He might complain while doing it, but still!

00:04:53.940 --> 00:04:57.470
Maybe he actually likes teaching
 and looking after people.

00:04:58.020 --> 00:05:00.020
Focus on the work at hand.

00:05:02.700 --> 00:05:04.110
By the way, Shinomiya-senpai,

00:05:04.600 --> 00:05:07.200
what made you decide to open a new restaurant?

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:09.080
And why in Japan?

00:05:09.450 --> 00:05:15.290
I read in <i>Tohtsuki Spotlight</i> that it's rare to open a new restaurant when you're trying to get three Michelin stars.

00:05:15.290 --> 00:05:17.750
And what did you mean earlier?

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:18.680
Huh?

00:05:18.680 --> 00:05:21.770
About being lucky that you 
can train at my restaurant?

00:05:21.770 --> 00:05:26.260
It would've been easier to pass the Stagiaire if
 you'd been assigned to a small local restaurant.

00:05:26.930 --> 00:05:28.800
I need to come up with a specialty.

00:05:29.680 --> 00:05:32.310
I can't stay the way I am now.

00:05:32.680 --> 00:05:35.400
I have to take one step forward

00:05:35.400 --> 00:05:38.560
and shine a new light on my cooking.

00:05:39.900 --> 00:05:41.070
Break time!

00:05:41.070 --> 00:05:42.330
I'm exhausted.

00:05:42.330 --> 00:05:44.760
We can finally see the light
 at the end of the tunnel, though.

00:05:44.760 --> 00:05:46.240
What should we do for lunch?

00:05:46.240 --> 00:05:47.870
I'll make something—

00:05:47.870 --> 00:05:48.860
I'll do it.

00:05:49.240 --> 00:05:49.740
What?

00:05:49.740 --> 00:05:51.720
Chef Shinomiya will cook for us?

00:05:51.720 --> 00:05:53.620
What's going on here?

00:05:53.620 --> 00:05:55.620
Set the table, will you?

00:05:56.120 --> 00:05:59.380
We'll get to eat Chef Shinomiya's staff lunch!

00:06:02.800 --> 00:06:04.360
<i>Mincing chicken!</i>

00:06:05.570 --> 00:06:09.760
Carefully saute mushrooms, hen-of-the-woods, and shimeji with butter.

00:06:10.190 --> 00:06:15.350
Then pour in an appareil made from eggs, soy milk,
 and white miso into a mold lined with pie crust dough.

00:06:21.270 --> 00:06:23.230
Wow, it looks delicious!

00:06:23.770 --> 00:06:25.480
What is this dish called?

00:06:25.480 --> 00:06:26.790
It's a quiche.

00:06:26.790 --> 00:06:29.570
It's originally a regional dish from Lorraine,

00:06:29.570 --> 00:06:31.990
and a typical lunch menu item, even in Paris.

00:06:32.380 --> 00:06:35.660
Not that you'd know, 
since you're not familiar with France.

00:06:35.660 --> 00:06:37.670
Oh, I see!

00:06:37.670 --> 00:06:39.460
It's perfect for a staff lunch too.

00:06:39.850 --> 00:06:40.880
Thanks for the food!

00:06:40.880 --> 00:06:43.000
<i>I'll savor it.</i>

00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:44.750
<i>The magic of legumes...</i>

00:06:47.920 --> 00:06:50.850
<i>What is this crunchiness?!</i>

00:06:55.880 --> 00:06:56.930
Burdock root, right?

00:06:56.930 --> 00:06:58.140
Bur-what?

00:06:58.140 --> 00:07:00.450
It's no wonder you don't know.

00:07:00.450 --> 00:07:03.150
The ingredient tends to be avoided in the West.

00:07:03.800 --> 00:07:06.530
<i>The crunchy texture of thinly-shaved burdock root</i>

00:07:06.530 --> 00:07:08.710
<i>combines with the melted cheese.</i>

00:07:08.710 --> 00:07:12.740
<i>It pairs well with the juicy chicken
 and the black pepper too!</i>

00:07:13.150 --> 00:07:16.490
How'd he achieve such deep flavors without even using bouillon?

00:07:16.490 --> 00:07:20.790
He extracted the sweetness and bitterness from the skin of the burdock root in perfect balance,

00:07:20.790 --> 00:07:23.750
to provide an edge to the mellow flavors of the chicken and cheese.

00:07:24.090 --> 00:07:27.960
Combining Japanese ingredients in this way into a regional French dish!

00:07:27.960 --> 00:07:30.090
This dish is good enough to serve at the main SHINO'S restaurant!

00:07:30.590 --> 00:07:33.140
No wonder you're the Magician of Legumes!

00:07:38.050 --> 00:07:39.680
Damn, I've still got a long way to go.

00:07:40.600 --> 00:07:42.560
All right, let's open up some wine!

00:07:42.560 --> 00:07:43.320
What?!

00:07:43.320 --> 00:07:44.860
Aren't we barely within budget?

00:07:44.860 --> 00:07:47.190
This is my cooking.

00:07:47.190 --> 00:07:49.570
It'll go to waste if we don't pair it with wine.

00:07:49.570 --> 00:07:51.070
Got it!

00:07:51.670 --> 00:07:53.690
Idiot, bring better wine!

00:07:53.690 --> 00:07:54.700
Okay, sorry!

00:07:55.920 --> 00:07:57.660
<i>After making something this good,</i>

00:07:57.660 --> 00:07:59.410
<i>he still thinks it's not good enough?</i>

00:08:00.020 --> 00:08:00.870
Yukihira.

00:08:01.160 --> 00:08:05.460
You will get closer to your own specialty over the course of this week.

00:08:05.960 --> 00:08:09.890
That is, if you can keep up with the work I require until the end.

00:08:09.890 --> 00:08:12.560
Are you prepared, 
Monsieur Yukihira?

00:08:12.560 --> 00:08:13.550
Yep!

00:08:19.310 --> 00:08:21.320
It suits you better than I thought it would.

00:08:21.320 --> 00:08:22.600
What do you mean, better than you thought?

00:08:22.600 --> 00:08:24.440
The chef's uniform.

00:08:24.440 --> 00:08:26.110
And here I thought I'd get a laugh out of you.

00:08:27.520 --> 00:08:28.110
Oh, well.

00:08:28.590 --> 00:08:30.540
It's almost time for the pre-open.

00:08:30.540 --> 00:08:31.560
Don't fall behind.

00:08:31.560 --> 00:08:32.030
Yep!

00:08:34.630 --> 00:08:38.470
By the way, what's the difference between the pre-open and the actual open?

00:08:38.470 --> 00:08:39.080
Let's see.

00:08:39.590 --> 00:08:43.040
Basically, it's a practice run before the official open.

00:08:43.510 --> 00:08:45.760
You invite mostly people you know,

00:08:45.760 --> 00:08:49.920
and check how well the staff are working together while serving guests food.

00:08:49.920 --> 00:08:50.630
Ah...

00:08:50.630 --> 00:08:52.240
I see.

00:08:52.240 --> 00:08:56.520
Also, it's partly to test the new 
menu of SHINO'S Tokyo.

00:08:56.520 --> 00:09:00.320
We'll be changing dishes every day
 while checking how the guests respond.

00:09:00.320 --> 00:09:03.770
On the final day, we'll have a staff competition for new menu items.

00:09:03.770 --> 00:09:04.770
A competition!

00:09:04.770 --> 00:09:05.850
Yukihira!

00:09:05.850 --> 00:09:07.650
You're done with your assigned tasks?

00:09:07.650 --> 00:09:09.110
Oh, yeah.

00:09:09.110 --> 00:09:10.640
I peeled everything

00:09:10.640 --> 00:09:12.430
and made lobster bouillon.

00:09:12.430 --> 00:09:14.950
Oh, I've also already marinated octopus and daikon root for half a day.

00:09:14.950 --> 00:09:20.120
Good! Yukihira, you'll be my assistant for now.

00:09:20.120 --> 00:09:23.200
Once you get used to the work, 
you might also become Abel-san's assistant.

00:09:23.200 --> 00:09:25.120
Okay, I'll try my best!

00:09:25.970 --> 00:09:28.790
<i>In the pre-open, three courses 
will be available for order.</i>

00:09:28.790 --> 00:09:31.340
<i>Depending on the course, 
a different main dish is served,</i>

00:09:31.340 --> 00:09:33.260
<i>or more amuses-bouches are served.</i>

00:09:33.820 --> 00:09:38.720
<i>Well, either way, it's easy when you know every dish that needs to be prepared.</i>

00:09:38.720 --> 00:09:41.100
Shinomiya-san, it's been too long!

00:09:41.100 --> 00:09:42.470
Welcome.

00:09:42.470 --> 00:09:44.020
Thank you for coming.

00:09:44.590 --> 00:09:46.810
<i>The first customer has arrived.</i>

00:09:46.810 --> 00:09:48.280
<i>I should get in position—</i>

00:09:50.420 --> 00:09:52.650
<i>What's with this sudden tension?</i>

00:09:55.610 --> 00:09:57.530
Please watch over me, O Lord.

00:09:58.350 --> 00:09:59.950
The customer has been seated.

00:09:59.950 --> 00:10:00.700
Let's go.

00:10:02.080 --> 00:10:03.290
Oui, Chef!

00:10:05.290 --> 00:10:08.060
<i>So fast! Yet so quiet!</i>

00:10:08.920 --> 00:10:11.880
<i>I can only hear the sound of knives 
and the simmering of the soup.</i>

00:10:13.360 --> 00:10:15.010
Don't make any unnecessary noise.

00:10:15.010 --> 00:10:16.760
Next time that happens, 
I'll be kicking you out.

00:10:18.510 --> 00:10:19.850
<i>I see.</i>

00:10:19.850 --> 00:10:22.510
<i>It's so you don't miss 
any minute change in sound.</i>

00:10:27.350 --> 00:10:29.060
Table 1's amuse-bouche is ready.

00:10:29.060 --> 00:10:29.810
Oui!

00:10:30.250 --> 00:10:32.520
<i>It's different from any other 
kitchen I've experienced!</i>

00:10:47.020 --> 00:10:48.230
So delicious!

00:10:48.230 --> 00:10:49.830
It's just as good as its reputation!

00:10:49.830 --> 00:10:51.330
He's indeed a magician!

00:10:52.080 --> 00:10:53.340
The hors d'oeuvres are ready.

00:10:53.340 --> 00:10:54.090
Oui!

00:10:54.090 --> 00:10:55.460
For Table 2 next.

00:10:55.460 --> 00:10:57.090
Four guests for Table 3.

00:10:57.090 --> 00:10:58.470
Orders for Table 4.

00:10:59.340 --> 00:11:01.300
Yukihira, don't fall behind.

00:11:01.300 --> 00:11:03.300
Quietly strain that fumet de poisson.

00:11:03.300 --> 00:11:04.180
Hurry.

00:11:04.180 --> 00:11:04.720
Got it!

00:11:05.210 --> 00:11:06.520
<i>The workload is huge.</i>

00:11:06.520 --> 00:11:10.190
<i>Even one prep work task has many more steps than a diner dish would need.</i>

00:11:10.190 --> 00:11:12.320
<i>In addition, while we're making appetizers,</i>

00:11:12.320 --> 00:11:15.270
<i>we have to start preparing
 the time-consuming main dishes.</i>

00:11:15.270 --> 00:11:16.730
Yukihira, langoustine!

00:11:16.730 --> 00:11:19.950
<i>Um, langoustines are... Norway lobsters!</i>

00:11:19.950 --> 00:11:20.570
Here you go!

00:11:20.570 --> 00:11:23.530
Also, prepare a mirepoix ready to go by around the time Table 3 finishes eating.

00:11:23.530 --> 00:11:24.930
<i>Mirepoix...</i>

00:11:24.930 --> 00:11:27.380
<i>Diced aromatic vegetables.</i>

00:11:27.380 --> 00:11:29.210
<i>Shit. I'm deciding so slowly.</i>

00:11:29.710 --> 00:11:31.620
<i>But I can manage to keep up, just barely.</i>

00:11:31.620 --> 00:11:33.800
<i>Table 3 just got their appetizer,</i>

00:11:33.800 --> 00:11:36.380
<i>so I need to start with prepping the fish for Table 1.</i>

00:11:37.840 --> 00:11:38.990
Yukihira!

00:11:38.990 --> 00:11:40.090
Where's the mirepoix?!

00:11:40.720 --> 00:11:42.950
<i>Table 3's already finished!</i>

00:11:42.950 --> 00:11:43.550
<i>Crap!</i>

00:11:43.550 --> 00:11:44.760
Sorry, it's not ready yet!

00:11:46.090 --> 00:11:47.350
<i>In a course menu,</i>

00:11:47.350 --> 00:11:51.030
<i>it's an ironclad rule to serve the next dish when
 everyone at the table has finished the current dish.</i>

00:11:51.030 --> 00:11:52.820
<i>You have to match the pace of the guests</i>

00:11:52.820 --> 00:11:55.900
<i>and adjust when you'll serve the next dish.</i>

00:11:55.900 --> 00:11:57.440
<i>There are multiple tables,</i>

00:11:57.440 --> 00:11:59.410
<i>and they all arrived at different times.</i>

00:11:59.410 --> 00:12:01.370
<i>If you rush to prep for one table,</i>

00:12:01.370 --> 00:12:03.910
<i>a different table will sneak up on you!</i>

00:12:03.910 --> 00:12:06.620
Yukihira, start prepping the mirepoix right away.

00:12:06.990 --> 00:12:09.210
Lucie, delay Table 3's order!

00:12:09.210 --> 00:12:10.830
Prepare Table 1's fish first!

00:12:10.830 --> 00:12:11.460
Oui!

00:12:11.460 --> 00:12:14.770
Wei, Table 3's meat dish will be delayed five minutes.

00:12:14.770 --> 00:12:16.000
Go explain to the customers.

00:12:16.000 --> 00:12:16.710
Oui!

00:12:16.710 --> 00:12:19.670
Abel, clean up after Yukihira's mistake.

00:12:20.010 --> 00:12:21.130
Oui, Chef.

00:12:21.130 --> 00:12:23.430
I'll assist Table 1's order.

00:12:23.430 --> 00:12:24.010
Step aside.

00:12:24.010 --> 00:12:24.680
Got it.

00:12:25.260 --> 00:12:26.790
<i>Instead of helping Abel-san,</i>

00:12:26.790 --> 00:12:28.060
<i>I held him up instead.</i>

00:12:28.680 --> 00:12:32.480
<i>Until now, if I've fallen behind, I've just had to worry about catching up on my own.</i>

00:12:33.050 --> 00:12:38.860
<i>But here, if I fall behind, I'll affect everyone involved in preparing the course menu!</i>

00:12:39.300 --> 00:12:40.370
I'll say this.

00:12:40.370 --> 00:12:43.240
I haven't accepted you as one of the team.

00:12:43.240 --> 00:12:43.990
Abel!

00:12:43.990 --> 00:12:45.320
What, you disagree?

00:12:45.830 --> 00:12:48.120
We don't need anyone who'll slow down the kitchen's workflow.

00:12:48.540 --> 00:12:50.510
I'm the head chef of SHINO'S Tokyo.

00:12:50.510 --> 00:12:52.250
I have a responsibility to manage the work.

00:12:52.700 --> 00:12:55.250
Now you know.
 In the end, you're just part of the Stagiaire.

00:12:55.790 --> 00:12:57.920
Don't get arrogant and think 
you've made it into the team.

00:12:58.310 --> 00:12:59.590
Now that you get it, 
know your place—

00:12:59.590 --> 00:13:01.090
Sorry, I'll be right back!

00:13:07.640 --> 00:13:09.140
<i>The pre-open lasts five days.</i>

00:13:09.140 --> 00:13:10.890
<i>I can't leave like this!</i>

00:13:11.250 --> 00:13:12.270
Sorry to keep you waiting!

00:13:12.750 --> 00:13:16.290
<i>I'm going to become a core 
member by the last day!</i>

00:14:03.580 --> 00:14:05.010
Hey, where are the ingredients?!

00:14:05.010 --> 00:14:05.610
Hurry up!

00:14:05.610 --> 00:14:06.400
Sorry!

00:14:06.400 --> 00:14:08.320
No, you've failed.

00:14:08.320 --> 00:14:09.160
What?!

00:14:09.160 --> 00:14:11.080
You failed.

00:14:11.080 --> 00:14:11.800
Fail!

00:14:13.270 --> 00:14:15.160
You can use the staff shower anytime you want.

00:14:15.160 --> 00:14:17.790
The kitchen staff usually arrive around noon,

00:14:17.790 --> 00:14:20.330
so take care of personal matters until then.

00:14:20.330 --> 00:14:21.760
Don't oversleep, no matter what.

00:14:21.760 --> 00:14:22.920
Got it.

00:14:22.920 --> 00:14:25.790
Based on how you worked today,

00:14:25.790 --> 00:14:27.760
it'd be better if you didn't stay, really.

00:14:28.510 --> 00:14:32.300
My success in Japan depends on the pre-open.

00:14:32.680 --> 00:14:36.150
You may not feel the pressure,
 being a student and all.

00:14:36.150 --> 00:14:36.810
Am I wrong?

00:14:37.960 --> 00:14:40.550
I plan to bring in more customers starting tomorrow.

00:14:40.550 --> 00:14:43.520
The workload will increase two or three-fold.

00:14:44.020 --> 00:14:49.680
Unless you change,
 you won't be here by the last day.

00:14:51.500 --> 00:14:52.990
Chef Shinomiya!

00:14:52.990 --> 00:14:55.620
You're not going to give him any advice?

00:14:55.620 --> 00:14:58.200
I don't have time to hold his hand.

00:14:58.200 --> 00:14:59.240
Besides...

00:15:01.150 --> 00:15:02.960
No, never mind.

00:15:06.010 --> 00:15:07.850
<i>Yukihira, don't fall behind.</i>

00:15:07.850 --> 00:15:10.050
<i>Quietly strain that fumet de poisson.</i>

00:15:10.050 --> 00:15:11.280
<i>No, no!</i>

00:15:11.280 --> 00:15:13.810
<i>This recette requires 
the ingredients to be julienned!</i>

00:15:13.810 --> 00:15:14.430
<i>Redo!</i>

00:15:14.430 --> 00:15:16.640
<i>If you do it again, I'll kick you out.</i>

00:15:19.440 --> 00:15:21.440
<i>Is it delicious, or disgusting?</i>

00:15:21.440 --> 00:15:22.560
<i>Tell me!</i>

00:15:23.180 --> 00:15:24.860
<i>Enjoy!</i>

00:15:40.880 --> 00:15:41.670
<i>My own...</i>

00:15:42.460 --> 00:15:44.080
<i>unique...</i>

00:15:44.900 --> 00:15:45.950
<i>cooking.</i>

00:15:52.220 --> 00:15:55.820
There are three possible ways to cut the 
potatoes that are served with this recette:

00:15:55.820 --> 00:15:58.680
pont neuf, allumette, and paille.

00:15:58.680 --> 00:16:01.140
The thickness and the 
length of each type differ.

00:16:01.140 --> 00:16:02.870
As for how to cut fish,

00:16:02.870 --> 00:16:06.160
there's médaillon, darne, 
tronçon, and escalope.

00:16:06.160 --> 00:16:09.150
I have to differentiate between them
 based on the ingredients and the dish.

00:16:11.030 --> 00:16:12.610
Good morning, Abel-san!

00:16:12.610 --> 00:16:14.090
Good morning, Lucie.

00:16:16.280 --> 00:16:17.370
Good morning!

00:16:18.120 --> 00:16:18.990
Yukihira?

00:16:18.990 --> 00:16:20.390
You're here early.

00:16:20.390 --> 00:16:21.080
Hi!

00:16:21.540 --> 00:16:26.710
Um, so I had questions about how to cut ingredients, the ones I messed up yesterday.

00:16:26.710 --> 00:16:28.510
May I ask you for your time?

00:16:28.510 --> 00:16:30.800
We have to clean and prep ingredients.

00:16:31.300 --> 00:16:35.800
You've got some nerve asking
 after holding us back yesterday, huh?

00:16:36.310 --> 00:16:39.570
The restaurant can't waste any more on you—

00:16:38.310 --> 00:16:39.570
Abel-san!

00:16:45.150 --> 00:16:48.920
The cleaning and peeling... 
Everything's done.

00:16:51.390 --> 00:16:52.270
Lucie.

00:16:52.270 --> 00:16:54.220
Answer Yukihira's questions.

00:16:54.220 --> 00:16:55.410
S-Sure!

00:16:55.410 --> 00:16:56.990
What do you want to know, Yukihira?

00:16:56.990 --> 00:16:59.530
Oh, about the different cutting techniques...

00:16:59.530 --> 00:17:02.330
I get that médaillon 
and darne basically look like this,

00:16:59.820 --> 00:17:02.330
<i>He did all this work by himself?</i>

00:17:02.330 --> 00:17:05.290
but should tronçon 
and escalope {basically }look like {this and that}these?

00:17:02.850 --> 00:17:05.290
<i>Did he even get any sleep?</i>

00:17:05.290 --> 00:17:08.750
Oh, well tronçon is like this. Get it?

00:17:15.680 --> 00:17:16.670
No good!

00:17:16.670 --> 00:17:17.300
Redo!

00:17:17.300 --> 00:17:18.680
Sorry, right away!

00:17:18.680 --> 00:17:19.810
You have 20 seconds.

00:17:19.810 --> 00:17:20.730
Got it!

00:17:20.730 --> 00:17:22.100
Yukihira, ingredients!

00:17:22.100 --> 00:17:24.270
Sorry, I'll get right to it 
after I'm done with this!

00:17:34.530 --> 00:17:36.930
Isn't that kind of like an hors d'oeuvre?

00:17:36.930 --> 00:17:38.490
Okay, I'll make it an entrée.

00:17:42.200 --> 00:17:43.900
Too slow! Faster next time!

00:17:43.900 --> 00:17:44.660
Got it!

00:18:01.150 --> 00:18:02.060
Again?

00:18:02.060 --> 00:18:03.810
This is three days in a row.

00:18:03.810 --> 00:18:06.940
Yeah, I'm really sorry to bother you like this.

00:18:06.940 --> 00:18:10.810
So today I have about fifty questions!

00:18:11.440 --> 00:18:13.070
I can help.

00:18:13.070 --> 00:18:14.900
Um, it's about this.

00:18:14.900 --> 00:18:17.640
Oh, you did it just like I taught you.

00:18:17.640 --> 00:18:19.870
There are about three things I want to improve.

00:18:19.870 --> 00:18:20.610
What about?

00:18:20.220 --> 00:18:21.330
<i>Yukihira...</i>

00:18:20.610 --> 00:18:21.330
First off...

00:18:21.760 --> 00:18:24.160
<i>How can he stay so unfazed</i>

00:18:22.590 --> 00:18:24.160
<i>No, no, no!</i>

00:18:24.160 --> 00:18:26.870
So my way is fine, then.

00:18:24.160 --> 00:18:26.870
<i>after being berated day after day?</i>

00:18:26.870 --> 00:18:29.040
You can figure out the rest on your own.

00:18:27.360 --> 00:18:31.040
<i>He should be painfully 
aware of how useless he is.</i>

00:18:29.040 --> 00:18:29.950
Got it!

00:18:31.680 --> 00:18:33.050
<i>Why isn't he dejected?</i>

00:18:38.090 --> 00:18:41.680
Yes, tomorrow is the last 
day of our pre-open event.

00:18:46.860 --> 00:18:47.640
All right!

00:18:48.090 --> 00:18:48.600
Yukihira—

00:18:49.170 --> 00:18:51.480
The fish for Table 8, right?

00:18:51.480 --> 00:18:52.730
The prep work's all done.

00:18:53.710 --> 00:18:54.820
Merci!

00:18:58.240 --> 00:19:00.230
Finished with prepping the scorpionfish.

00:19:00.230 --> 00:19:01.320
Please check!

00:19:01.700 --> 00:19:03.280
Finished with deglazing the suc.

00:19:03.740 --> 00:19:05.240
Finished with making champignon tourné.

00:19:05.620 --> 00:19:07.500
Finishing with mincing shallots. Please check!

00:19:07.500 --> 00:19:08.830
It's fine. Good work.

00:19:08.830 --> 00:19:10.600
Yukihira, Table 6's next!

00:19:10.600 --> 00:19:11.170
Got it!

00:19:11.780 --> 00:19:14.330
<i>I don't have even a second 
to feel sorry for myself.</i>

00:19:14.330 --> 00:19:19.840
<i>Because I'm having way too much fun mastering new techniques!</i>

00:19:25.420 --> 00:19:27.200
<i>He's absorbing it all!</i>

00:19:27.200 --> 00:19:29.480
<i>With incredible force and speed!</i>

00:19:30.210 --> 00:19:32.560
Table 4's quickly working through their course!

00:19:32.560 --> 00:19:33.690
Can we hurry up their soup?

00:19:33.690 --> 00:19:34.500
<i>Damn!</i>

00:19:34.500 --> 00:19:35.900
<i>I'm not done with the prep work.</i>

00:19:35.900 --> 00:19:37.610
Abel, can you handle it?

00:19:37.610 --> 00:19:38.600
Sorry!

00:19:38.600 --> 00:19:39.740
I can't right now.

00:19:39.740 --> 00:19:41.110
I'm busy here too!

00:19:42.440 --> 00:19:43.870
The prep work's done.

00:19:44.620 --> 00:19:45.780
Yukihira.

00:19:45.780 --> 00:19:47.450
You've memorized the recette, haven't you?

00:19:47.830 --> 00:19:49.410
Finish the dish.

00:19:53.520 --> 00:19:54.330
Got it!

00:19:54.330 --> 00:19:56.990
Well, that was the best 
food I've ever tasted!

00:19:54.800 --> 00:19:56.490
I'm glad I could check it 
out during the pre-open.

00:19:56.490 --> 00:19:58.900
Once it opens, we won't be 
able to make a reservation.

00:19:56.990 --> 00:19:59.800
I'd like to bring a few friends next time.

00:20:01.410 --> 00:20:02.720
Good work, everyone!

00:20:03.570 --> 00:20:05.350
The pre-open ends tomorrow.

00:20:05.720 --> 00:20:09.350
Don't slack on the last day, Yukihira.

00:20:09.350 --> 00:20:10.680
Of course not.

00:20:10.680 --> 00:20:12.960
Good job, Yukihira!

00:20:12.960 --> 00:20:13.560
Thanks!

00:20:13.990 --> 00:20:17.520
Abel, do you object 
to keeping Yukihira around?

00:20:18.320 --> 00:20:19.860
No.

00:20:19.860 --> 00:20:22.320
Well, I suppose he gets 
passing marks right now.

00:20:22.700 --> 00:20:25.780
I was really worried for a while.

00:20:25.780 --> 00:20:27.950
You didn't give him any advice.

00:20:27.950 --> 00:20:30.040
There's no point if he can't 
figure it out on his own.

00:20:30.830 --> 00:20:31.960
<i>Besides...</i>

00:20:31.960 --> 00:20:34.290
<i>Shinomiya-senpai, 
I'm sorry to bother you,</i>

00:20:34.290 --> 00:20:35.540
<i>but I have one more thing.</i>

00:20:35.540 --> 00:20:38.190
<i>Yes, Monsieur Yukihira?</i>

00:20:38.190 --> 00:20:39.630
<i>Do you have another complaint?</i>

00:20:39.630 --> 00:20:44.340
<i>Does that Tohtsuki rule apply to alumni too?</i>

00:20:45.150 --> 00:20:46.220
<i>What are you talking about?</i>

00:20:47.180 --> 00:20:48.100
<i>A Cooking Battle.</i>

00:20:50.840 --> 00:20:52.680
<i>If I beat you in a Cooking Battle,</i>

00:20:53.160 --> 00:20:56.930
<i>will you rescind Tadokoro's expulsion?</i>

00:20:59.590 --> 00:21:02.860
<i>You challenged </i>me<i>, of all people.</i>

00:21:03.600 --> 00:21:06.360
<i>You wouldn't fail at something like the Stagiaire.</i>

00:21:14.090 --> 00:21:15.250
<i>I lost.</i>

00:21:15.250 --> 00:21:16.370
<i>I lost.</i>

00:21:16.370 --> 00:21:17.670
<i>I lost.</i>

00:21:19.440 --> 00:21:20.710
<i>Damn it!</i>

00:21:23.220 --> 00:21:24.630
Shinomiya-senpai!

00:21:24.630 --> 00:21:26.990
Sorry, do you have a minute?

00:21:26.990 --> 00:21:28.010
What, Yukihira?

00:21:28.010 --> 00:21:29.820
Do you have a complaint?

00:21:29.820 --> 00:21:30.350
No.

00:21:31.120 --> 00:21:34.560
Since it looks like I'm allowed to stay until the last day, I have a request.

00:21:35.120 --> 00:21:36.060
What is it?

00:21:37.350 --> 00:21:37.940
The competition.

00:21:39.240 --> 00:21:43.430
There'll be a new menu item competition
 after the restaurant closes tomorrow, right?

00:21:43.430 --> 00:21:45.150
I want to submit a dish too.

00:21:45.150 --> 00:21:46.080
What?!

00:21:46.080 --> 00:21:47.100
The competition?

00:21:47.100 --> 00:21:49.660
But you've had your hands full assisting us!

00:21:50.910 --> 00:21:52.160
Yukihira!

00:21:52.160 --> 00:21:54.790
No, I always planned on participating 
in the competition.

00:21:55.840 --> 00:22:00.710
I want to make everything I've envisioned until now into a reality as soon as I can.

00:22:05.680 --> 00:22:08.160
Will it be anything decent?

00:22:08.160 --> 00:22:08.760
Yes.

00:22:08.760 --> 00:22:12.990
Come to think of it, it'll be the first time I taste an original recette of yours.

00:22:12.990 --> 00:22:13.470
Yep.

00:22:13.870 --> 00:22:15.680
Very well.

00:22:15.680 --> 00:22:20.940
But I won't guarantee that your hard-won confidence will survive this.

00:22:22.630 --> 00:22:24.990
<i>I swear I'll make him speechless...</i>

00:22:25.430 --> 00:22:26.860
<i>with a dish only I can make.</i>

00:22:27.590 --> 00:22:30.960
<i>With my specialty!</i>

00:22:57.260 --> 00:23:02.140
An intensely burning desire was born

00:23:02.140 --> 00:23:07.980
But not in me, in someone else

00:23:07.980 --> 00:23:12.780
Where's the me who believed that

00:23:12.780 --> 00:23:17.910
All one needs is to have hopes and dreams

00:23:17.910 --> 00:23:23.160
Wrapped around something long, my compass was lost

00:23:23.160 --> 00:23:28.920
On the border of life and death, snow drops bloom

00:23:28.920 --> 00:23:34.260
If by some mistake they get smashed

00:23:34.260 --> 00:23:39.430
At least put flowers on the empty husk

00:23:39.430 --> 00:23:45.100
Is that the way things are? Yes, it is

00:23:45.100 --> 00:23:50.150
You can call it resignation if you want

00:23:50.150 --> 00:23:56.070
But that's not me, that's not me

00:23:56.070 --> 00:24:00.700
There's no value in something just anyone could make

00:24:06.250 --> 00:24:09.960
Final episode, "Pomp and Circumstance."
